Learning what (not) to eat is going to be very important, particularly
if you go with this strategy.  It's worth trying to figure out what
you can always eat (unless you're already too stuffed), what you can
never eat, and what you can eat sometimes (and when!)  Remember, the
dungeon is not a refrigerator.
Some people recommend playing barbarians at the start for this reason,
you'll soon figure out why.
On the other hand, if you let the game pick random roles, or vary the
roles you pick, you may die more often, but learn more from each
death.

If you come across an altar, try and find out what it's good for (the
most useful things may not be the most obvious thing).


